1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:04,799
Noah caught some air in a jar.

2
00:00:04,929 --> 00:00:06,986
Look: it's transparent.

3
00:00:08,398 --> 00:00:10,019
So why does the air look blue,

4
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:10,985
way up high?

5
00:00:12,406 --> 00:00:13,747
Mila has an idea:

6
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:15,901
the sky is a mirror of the sea!

7
00:00:16,037 --> 00:00:17,091
Above the desert…

8
00:00:17,141 --> 00:00:18,082
still blue.

9
00:00:18,204 --> 00:00:19,664
It's not a reflection.

10
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:21,719
Discovery mission!

11
00:00:25,328 --> 00:00:27,005
Sunlight looks white.

12
00:00:27,149 --> 00:00:28,934
But it hides all the colors.

13
00:00:30,314 --> 00:00:32,127
Red makes big waves.

14
00:00:32,298 --> 00:00:34,355
Blue makes tiny, tight ones.

15
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:36,680
Mini mode!

16
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:38,451
Air is made of tiny beads,

17
00:00:38,501 --> 00:00:40,493
with lots of empty space between them.

18
00:00:41,201 --> 00:00:43,561
The big red waves go almost straight through.

19
00:00:43,675 --> 00:00:46,151
The little blue waves bounce off the beads,

20
00:00:46,201 --> 00:00:47,558
in every direction!

21
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:49,954
And since there is air everywhere,

22
00:00:50,004 --> 00:00:51,681
blue gets scattered everywhere.

23
00:00:51,797 --> 00:00:52,744
Wherever you look,

24
00:00:52,794 --> 00:00:54,597
a bit of blue reaches your eyes.

25
00:00:55,442 --> 00:00:57,037
That's why the sky is blue.

26
00:01:00,442 --> 00:01:03,151
The air scatters blue all across the sky.

27
00:01:04,927 --> 00:01:06,698
With an adult: a lamp,

28
00:01:06,748 --> 00:01:09,246
a glass of water, two drops of milk.

29
00:01:09,381 --> 00:01:11,839
From the side, the light turns blue!

30
00:01:12,568 --> 00:01:13,795
And in the evening,

31
00:01:13,857 --> 00:01:15,618
why does the sky turn orange?

32
00:01:15,745 --> 00:01:17,076
The answer tomorrow.
